TODO list (incomplete)

This is a Bestechnic BES2600 / BEST2002 SDIO mac80211 driver (CW1200-family
WSM firmware protocol).  On PineTab2 v2.0 (RK3566, mmc2) STA Wi-Fi currently
works: firmware load, scan (idle and while associated), open and WPA2
associate, DHCP, ping, clean shutdown.  Bluetooth has never worked.

The driver was previously removed from staging for quality.  Do not send it
upstream until the items below are addressed enough that timeouts and RF
misses cannot oops the machine or flood WARN stacks.

Proven working (STA, PineTab2 v2.0, firmware Dec 2023)
-----------------------------------------------------
* Probe, boot + main firmware, phy registration.
* STA + P2P_DEVICE vifs (P2P is host-only; see below).
* Idle scan: 2.4 GHz then 5 GHz, firmware scan-complete status 0.
* Associated background scan (WSM_SCAN_TYPE_BACKGROUND +
  WSM_SCAN_FLAG_FORCE_BACKGROUND).  Do not restore FAST_PS after scan.
* Open (STARLINK) and WPA2-CCMP (NETGEAR) association, 4-way, DHCP, ping.
* BlockAck left off on the host; firmware owns BA.  Auto-enabling BA after
  HT ACKs produced "connected" with 0% ping (RX AMPDU).
* ICMP / DNS / DHCP / ARP pinned at 1 Mbps even after the first IP ACK.
* Do not force_close the SDIO bus on -EBUSY (hard-locks the SoC).
* Join with leftover hw_bufs_used=1: soft-clear, do not poke RX.

Do not regress those without a replacement that has been tested on hardware.

WARN_ON / BUG_ON
----------------
* Done for firmware/bus errors: WSM command failures, parse underflow,
  SDIO I/O, and "unexpected path" now use bes_fail()/bes_err() and return
  -Exxx.  BUG_ON is gone from .c files.
* Remaining WARN_ON are programmer invariants (NULL about to be
  dereferenced, queue id out of range, if_id == GENERIC, empty free
  pool).  Those still dump a stack on violation; that is intended.
* Re-audit if any leftover WARN_ON fires on a healthy associated STA
  session (it should not).

Logging
-------
* bes_pin() is printk(KERN_ERR ...) so it always hits the console.  Remove
  P51/P57/P59/P60 and other freeze-debug traces before any public patch.
* Hot-path bes_info() (scan start/complete, first TX/RX frames, set_pm)
  must become bes_devel() or go away.  Keep bes_err for real failures.
* global_dev in bes_log.h makes firmware-load lines print
  "(NULL device *)".  Bind logs to the SDIO function device.
* Firmware load still prints version/CRC at info level; fine for staging,
  too chatty for wireless.git later.

Power save / WSM 0x0010
-----------------------
* Firmware stays WSM_PSM_ACTIVE after join.  mac80211's desired mode is
  often FAST_PS (0x81).  Sending 0x0010 FAST_PS after associated scan
  blocked the RX path waiting for confirm: host scan timeout, ping still
  worked, shutdown stalled WPA on the same 0x0010 timeout.
* Do not wsm_set_pm() from BH/RX (scan_complete_cb).  Do not apply
  deferred FAST_PS in enter_lp_mode until it is proven on this firmware.
* Unjoin must drop join_status before releasing BES_PWR_LOCK_ON_PS_ACTIVE
  so teardown cannot fire 0x0010 while still STA.
* Only update firmware_ps_mode after 0x0010 confirms.

Scan
----
* Associated scans must use BACKGROUND + FORCE_BACKGROUND, never
  foreground 0x0007 while joined.
* Never wsm_reset() on 0x0007 failure while associated (drops the join).
* Never empty-scan reset while STA.
* Do not skip associated scans (that was a workaround for the 0x0010 hang).

Association / rates / aggregation
---------------------------------
* 5 GHz STARLINK BSS association at 6 Mbps often fails.  Diagnose; do not
  paper over with a second join hack without logs.
* Bulk TCP still uses MCS on a weak link while ICMP/DNS/DHCP are clamped
  to 1 Mbps.  Decide whether that clamp should apply more widely or go
  away once BA/rate control is trustworthy.
* Do not treat EAPOL ACK as data_acked (released the 1 Mbps clamp too
  early; DHCP/DNS went HT AMPDU).
* Firmware owns BlockAck.  Host ADDBA-Resp is dropped (tx_h_action).
  USE_HT_MODE at assoc re-arms FW BA; send BA policy off again after
  wsm_set_association_mode.  Do not auto-enable BA after HT ACKs.
* hw_bufs_used=1 before join still appears; soft-clear is enough for join
  to succeed.  Find the leaked buffer instead of only clearing the count.

MAC / interfaces
----------------
* Early MAC from addresses[0] is a dummy; stable MAC is derived from the
  SoC serial (02:00:00:3d:05:3c locally).  Dummy vs serial mismatch is
  confusing in dmesg; pick one story.
* P2P_DEVICE (nl80211 type 10) is advertised for printers / rare Direct.
  It is host-only: if_id=2 via addresses[1], no setup_mac_pvif, no extra
  0x0006 RCPI.  Do not update hw_priv->mac_addr except for if_id==0.
  DanctNIX 6.15 disabled P2P_DEVICE; keep or drop explicitly, do not
  leave a half-working vif that sends WSM on the STA if_id.
* hw_priv->mac_addr vs vif addresses vs LMAC station ID: keep them
  consistent on if_id=0; extra if_id=1 cfg is for combo firmware.

Bluetooth
---------
* Never worked on any kernel tried here.  CONFIG_BES2600_BT is off.
* Makefile still lists bes2600_btusb.o; that file is not in the tree.
* /dev/bes2600 (bes_chardev) is leftover vendor userspace control
  (echo ifname:bt cmd:BT_ON).  Either implement a real HCI path or
  document that BT is out of scope until then.
* UART hciattach on ttyS1 is the distro workaround; it is not this
  driver's job until the chip is actually taken out of Wi-Fi-only reset.

Hardware / firmware limits (not "just code")
--------------------------------------------
* PineTab2 does not wire BES2600 reset/power GPIOs the way the vendor
  EVB does.  Hard reset of a wedged chip needs a board power cycle.
  Do not assume gpio reset/powerup in platform_data.
* Firmware is proprietary (bes2600/best2002_fw_boot_sdio.bin +
  best2002_fw_sdio.bin, Dec 2023).  linux-firmware submission is a
  separate process; the driver must fail cleanly if blobs are missing.
* Factory calibration comes from bes2600_factory.txt.

Kconfig / build
---------------
* Drop unused platform variants if PineTab2 is the only in-tree user
  (Allwinner, Xiaomi R329, Sicun QM215, STE extensions, WAPI), or
  isolate them so the default PineTab2 config is obvious.
* GET_MAC_ADDR_METHOD as int 1-4 is not kernel style; use a proper
  choice or DT.
* Android-style default paths (/data/applog/, /data/cfg/) do not belong
  in a generic driver.
* Makefile still has out-of-tree bits: KERN_DIR, "all: modules",
  ccflags -Werror, hardcoded -DCHIP_WIFI_ROM_VER.  Staging build must
  be Kbuild-only.
* Mixed tabs/spaces (especially scan.c after later splits).  Run
  checkpatch.pl; many remaining hits will need real refactors, not
  line wraps.

Dead / leftover code
--------------------
* TODO:COMBO, HACK!!!, commented dump_stack(), #if 0, testmode / ITP /
  Xiaomi keepalive unless someone uses them.
* EPTA 0x0029 was a lockup source when piled on a sick bus after scan;
  do not send it from join-unlock without a proven need.
* SDIO TX bounce (tx_pad): do not DMA padded length from the skb.
  Keep that; document why.

Lockups already hit (do not reintroduce)
----------------------------------------
* force_close on SDIO CTRL/CMD53 -EBUSY (hard lock CPU / kworker).
* Nested 0x0006 operational-mode while MCU wake failed.
* Scan WARN-loop of 0x0006 / 0x0007 / 0x0029 after a sick bus; abort
  the scan instead.
* Host-only unjoin after failed auth skipped wsm_reset because RX was
  quiet; LMAC stayed joined; next 0x0007 returned status 13.
* BA timer used to clear ba_ena on low traffic and re-send
  BLOCK_ACK_POLICY every few seconds (ping jitter).  Timer is
  stats-only now.
* P2P add sending RCPI 0x0006 on if_id 0 racing CTRL -EBUSY.

Not this driver
---------------
* rockchip-drm swiotlb buffer full.
* QSampleCache wireless-extensions warning.
* systemd-journald "Time jumped backwards".
* typec-extcon / husb311 (megous / DanctNIX board patches, separate).

Contact / trees
---------------
* In-tree development: this directory on vendor-integration, based on
  a replay of v6.14.7-danctnix1 plus local STA fixes.
* Distro: DanctNIX linux-pinetab2 is now on Codeberg
  (https://codeberg.org/DanctNIX/linux-pinetab2), not the stale GitHub
  master.  Offer the STA delta against their current kernel; do not
  expect their tree to be the path into Linus.
* Mainline: linux-staging / wireless, patches against linux-next, with
  this file kept honest as items close.
